the derived rows-per-block shard rule as the DEFAULT — 2026-08-11
=================================================================
Branch  perf/bps-rows-default off main @ 52c61d9 (PR #502 merged).
        Timed binaries rebuilt at c2b5d0f, the LAST code-touching commit, and
        the whole t=8 table re-measured on them; the first pass (built at
        f97a168) is kept as ..._run1_... and agrees within 1.1% on every cell.
Box     Apple M4 Pro, 8P+4E, macOS, aarch64. Idle: foreign_max = 1 on the two
        wall sweeps (one row), 0 on the per-plane factorial.
Build   cargo --release, default features. No target-cpu=native.
        head  = DEFAULT build (the derived rows-per-block rule)
        base  = --features bps-blocks (the block-count rule shipped before this)
        half  = --features bps-half   (the best global constant on offer)
        untrk = --features probe-untracked (tracker-removed ceiling)
        pin   = --features probe-shiftpin, RAV1D_PIN_SHIFT="<stride>:<shift>,..."
Locks   every timed run under `measlock`. Builds/tests niced, timed runs never.
Fit     two-point, total = alpha + beta*frames, wall and user+sys separately,
        n_lo/n_hi PER CELL and never past the IVF's real length (checked by the
        harness, which fails loud). ROUNDS=8, ROUND 0 DISCARDED (first touch of
        each (arm,cell) is cold: a smoke read ms_lo 382 vs 326-330 warm). n=7.
        Ratios are PAIRED PER ROUND: v4k8tile drifts 47.5/50.6/48.9 ms/frame
        across rounds for ALL FIVE arms including dav1d, and that cancels in a
        paired ratio but not in a ratio of medians (6% band -> 1%).
Vectors ~/tmp/bpsrows/{vec,ivf} — 1:1 crops from mk_shardsize_vectors.sh (4x2 =
        8 tiles each), plus v4k_8tile and the 10-bit 1024x576 t8 ladder vector.
        All 10 bit-identical to dav1d 1.5.4 at t=1 AND t=8 on the final build
        BEFORE any timing (bps_rows_default_verify_2026-08-11.tsv).

IN-GRID NOISE CONTROLS (this is why the null cells are trustworthy)
   c256x2048 and v4k8tile: the derived rule computes the SAME shift as the
   block-count rule on every plane (verified off the tracker, shifts.tsv), so
   head and base are the same decoder there and the true ratio is exactly 1.000.
   Measured 0.9921 [0.9552..1.0175] and 1.0000 [0.9937..1.0093].
   Every cell at t=1 is the same kind of control (the rule is gated on
   tiles>=2 AND shards>=SHARDS_CONCURRENT): medians 0.9972-1.0004, all spanning 1.

