3. THE 512x576 PER-PLANE FACTORIAL (probe-shiftpin, n=7, foreign_max=0)
   paired wall vs pinL10C8 (= the block-count rule):
                 chroma 8   chroma 9   chroma 10
      luma 10      1.0000     0.9625      0.9918
      luma 11      0.9418     0.9213      0.9282   <- (11,10) IS the derived rule
      luma 12      0.9410     0.9184      0.9336   <- (12,10) = bps-half
   unpinned DEFAULT build in the same sweep: 0.9244 (vs its pinned twin 0.9282,
   0.4% — the instrument cross-checks).
   Additivity residual (measured / r(L,8)*r(10,C)): 1.0086 0.9909 1.0192 0.9943
   on wall, 0.9979 0.9920 0.9963 1.0026 on CPU. THE PLANES DO NOT INTERACT.
   #501's 0.995 "worse than both arms it sits between" DOES NOT REPRODUCE.
   Real residual: chroma is non-monotone (8->9 worth 3.75%, 9->10 gives most
   back at all three luma shifts) because ROWS_PER_BLOCK_MIN is one number for
   both planes while a 4:2:0 chroma tap window is half the luma one. Cost of the
   shared constant at this cell: ~0.7% vs bps1.

