   NEW: on every cell that moves, the rule lands the mean registration at
   3.2-3.9 ns = the census's UNCONTENDED t=1 rate (2.78-3.89). It removes
   essentially the whole contention premium there, not a slice of it.
   c1024x576 reads 529,092/frame against the cost census's 566,594 because #502
   landed in between; use this branch's counts with this branch's timings.

5. TIMER-FREE (probe-wide / __probe_bounds, both arms, all 8 cells, t=8 and t=1)
   * registration COUNT identical between arms on every cell
   * w_full = 0 on every row (the slot-exhaustion trap does not fire, including
     where the rule coarsens by three shifts)
   * multi/20f: 15,580->1,260 (c1024x192), 31,600->2,520 (c1024x384),
     72,680->21,320 (c3840x256), 34,910->23,582 (c1024x576),
     77,156->38,924 (10-bit); 0 in both arms at c512x576
   * CORRECTION to SHARD_GRANULARITY.md §1: the 153 all-shards promotions/frame
     at 1024x576 are NOT on a picture plane. This branch coarsens both planes by
     two shifts and w_shards stays 3,060/20f in both arms, while --features
     bps-1 (one shift on EVERY instance) takes it to 0. Coarsening is monotone,
     so if +1 everywhere removes them and +2 on the planes does not, they belong
     to a buffer with no declared stride. Unidentified; ~1 point of wall (#500 §5e).

NOT COVERED
   x86_64 (clippy target only), 4:4:4, 12-bit, film grain, inter/video content,
   `unchecked`, `asm`, t=2/4/16. One content class (photo), one quality point,
   all-intra, one key-frame OBU re-decoded. Loop restoration executes zero
   blocks on every cell. ROWS_PER_BLOCK_MIN = 4 is still fitted on #501's grid
   with no held-out size — __rpb_{2,8,16} is the ladder to re-fit it and was NOT
   swept here. msb-5 not bundled (~1%, not separated from zero). SLOTS untouched.
